### How do you find the employee closest to retirement?

```java
package com.bank.hr;

import java.util.*;

public class ClosestToRetirement {
    private static final int RETIREMENT_AGE = 60;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Employee> employees = Employee.getSampleEmployees();

        Optional<Employee> closest = employees.stream()
            .filter(e -> e.getAge() < RETIREMENT_AGE)
            .max(Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge));

        closest.ifPresent(e ->
            System.out.printf("%s, age %d, retires in %d years%n",
                e.getName(), e.getAge(),
                RETIREMENT_AGE - e.getAge()));
    }
}
```

```text
Suresh, age 58, retires in 2 years
```

### How do you list all employees retiring within 5 years?

```java
List<Employee> retiringWithin5 = employees.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getAge() >= RETIREMENT_AGE - 5
              && e.getAge() < RETIREMENT_AGE)
    .sorted(Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge).reversed())
    .toList();
```

### What are common mistakes?

Mistake: not excluding employees already at or past retirement age.

```java
// WRONG: includes employees already aged 60+
Optional<Employee> wrong = employees.stream()
    .max(Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge));
// Could return someone aged 62 who is already retired!

// CORRECT: filter first
Optional<Employee> correct = employees.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getAge() < RETIREMENT_AGE)
    .max(Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge));
```

### What about finding the closest to retirement per department?

```java
Map<String, Optional<Employee>> closestPerDept = employees.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getAge() < RETIREMENT_AGE)
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
        Employee::getDepartment,
        Collectors.maxBy(
            Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge))));
```

### What about listing employees retiring within N years?

```java
public static List<Employee> retiringWithin(
        List<Employee> employees, int years) {
    return employees.stream()
        .filter(e -> e.getAge() >= RETIREMENT_AGE - years
                  && e.getAge() < RETIREMENT_AGE)
        .sorted(Comparator.comparingInt(Employee::getAge).reversed())
        .toList();
}
```

### What about variable retirement age by role?

```java
Map<String, Integer> retirementAges = Map.of(
    "TRADING", 60, "OPERATIONS", 62, "RISK", 58);

Optional<Employee> closest = employees.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getAge() < retirementAges
        .getOrDefault(e.getDepartment(), 60))
    .max(Comparator.comparingInt(e ->
        e.getAge() - retirementAges
            .getOrDefault(e.getDepartment(), 60)));
```

### What are the edge cases?

If all employees are already past retirement age, the filter produces an empty stream and the result is Optional.empty(). An employee exactly at retirement age (age == 60) is excluded by the strict less-than filter.

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- "How do you find the closest to retirement per department?" Use groupingBy(dept, collectingAndThen(filtering(age < 60), maxBy(comparingInt(age)))).
- "What if retirement age varies by role?" Accept a Function<Employee, Integer> that maps each employee to their retirement age.
